From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:28:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 20/35] PROTOTYPE pco: keep branches with expensive ALU ops as
 branches

nir_opt_peephole_select was allowed to flatten if/else blocks of up to
64 instructions even when they contain transcendental ops. In
uber-shaders that select a code path by a uniform, such as KWin's
colour-management shader (one path per transfer function, each a few
pow()s), every pixel then executes all of the paths.

With expensive_alu_ok = false such blocks stay branches, which the USC
skips when no instance takes them. On an MT8173 (GX6250), KWin's
composite of a full-screen NV12 video went from 38.3 ms to 22.5 ms per
frame (20 to 30 fps presented); desktop drawer gestures unchanged.

Local experiment: Imagination's driver does not take LLM-written code.

Generated-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit c6529241cd1a07ee3c4b05793b3f9547ed5aa54d)
---
 src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c b/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c
index 0c7a1830474..bb273c9daf0 100644
--- a/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c
+++ b/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c
@@ -544,7 +544,7 @@ static void pco_nir_opt(pco_ctx *ctx, nir_shader *nir, pco_data *data, bool alge
       NIR_PASS(progress, nir, nir_opt_if, nir_opt_if_optimize_phi_true_false);
       nir_opt_peephole_select_options peep_opts = {
          .limit = 64,
-         .expensive_alu_ok = true,
+         .expensive_alu_ok = false,
       };
       NIR_PASS(progress, nir, nir_opt_peephole_select, &peep_opts);
 
